<title>JAPAN: Japan Oct green coffee imports up 19.1 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Oct green coffee imports up 19.1 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's green coffee imports in October totalled 33,428 tonnes, up by 19.1 percent from the same month a year earlier, according to Finance Ministry data released on Thursday.</p>
<p>Imports of roasted coffee amounted to 484 tonnes in October against 208 tonnes the same month a year earlier.</p>
<p>The breakdown is as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		   Oct 96	   Sept 96	  Oct 95</p>
<p> Total	   33,428	   29,181	   28,061</p>
<p> Indonesia	7,989	    5,167	    5,145</p>
<p> Colombia	 6,927	    6,572	    6,653</p>
<p> Brazil	   7,350	    6,363	    5,082</p>
<p> Guatemala	  652	    1,876	    1,421</p>
<p> Honduras	   564	    1,173		671</p>
<p>Cumulative green coffee imports in the first 10 months of 1996 were 276,072 tonnes against 263,700 tonnes in the same period of the previous year.</p>
<p>Roasted coffee imports (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    Oct 96	  Sept 96	   Oct 95</p>
<p>			 484	   487		 208</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +813 3432 7431</p>
</text>
